examples.code:
/* The new task form */

.new-task {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

input[type="text"] {
  min-inline-size: 0;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
}

.new-task input {
  flex: 1;
}

.task {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  min-block-size: 3rem;
  padding: 0.375rem 0.75rem;
}

.task + .task {
  border-block-start: 1px solid var(--line);
}

.task-toggle {
  flex: none;
  inline-size: 1.25rem;
  block-size: 1.25rem;
  margin: 0;
  accent-color: var(--accent);
}

.task-title {
  flex: 1;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

/* The footer */

.task-footer {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
  margin-block-start: 0.75rem;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  color: var(--muted);
}

.filters {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.25rem;
}

steps.body:
`display: grid` lays children out in rows and columns. Even with one column it earns its place: `place-items: center` centers content in both directions, and `gap` spaces a stack of items.

Fluid sizes adapt without breakpoints. `min(100%, 28rem)` is the full width on a phone and stops at 28rem on a wide screen. Use `rem` for sizes, so the layout grows when a user picks a larger font.

When the layout really must change, use a media query, and write it mobile first. The base rules are for the smallest screen, and each query adds to them as the screen gets wider:

```css
.cards { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }

@media (width >= 48rem) {
  .cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
}
```

Media queries also read the user's settings. `prefers-color-scheme` reports a dark or light theme, and `prefers-reduced-motion` reports that the user asked for less animation.

examples.code:
/* Layout */

.page {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  min-block-size: 100vh;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}

/* The card */

.card {
  inline-size: min(100%, 28rem);
  overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
}

:root {
  color-scheme: light dark;
  --font: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
  --bg: #f6f8fa;
  --surface: #ffffff;
  --text: #1f2328;
  --muted: #59636e;
  --line: #d1d9e0;
  --radius: 0.75rem;
  --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgb(31 35 40 / 0.06), 0 8px 24px rgb(31 35 40 / 0.08);
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --bg: #0d1117;
    --surface: #151b23;
    --text: #f0f6fc;
    --muted: #9198a1;
    --line: #3d444d;
    --shadow: 0 8px 24px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4);
  }
}

/* Reset */

*,
*::before,
*::after {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

body {
  margin: 0;
  font: 1rem/1.5 var(--font);
  color: var(--text);
  background: var(--bg);
}

h1,
p {
  margin: 0;
}

img,
picture {
  display: block;
  max-inline-size: 100%;
}
